<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    kuna issue testcase: a predicated ARM instruction's condition skip filed as
    a jump to the next instruction in the cross-reference index
    (`option armcondskip on|off`, default-ON).

    Issue:      kuna-analysis-armcondskip - `kuna xrefs` from any
                `movlt`/`ldrne`/`moveq` of an A32 or Thumb-2 image answered a
                Jump to the next instruction, which no other tool files.
    Stage:      P1 code/data partition - the on-demand cross-reference query
                (`listing/xrefs.rs`).
    P0 assert:  `option armcondskip on|off`.

    The Listing tier and the xref query are built only on the real-object
    bootstrap path, never on the console decompile path (docs/spec/
    01-program-prep.md section 1.6), and no console command prints an xref
    row, so a stage test cannot assert the row itself. This case pins what
    the console can show, as `kuna-picbase.xml` does for its option:

      * `option armcondskip off` parses and round-trips (an unknown option
        would make the console error and the next decompile would not run),
      * flipping it changes nothing in the rendered C of `clamp`, whose
        `movlt`/`movge` pair is the instruction shape the option concerns,
      * the catalog documents it as a default-on P1 option.

    The two-pass proof (option off = a Jump from every predicated instruction
    to the next one, default = none, real conditional branches keep theirs)
    lives in the cargo gate `decompiler/crates/kuna-console/tests/
    verify_xreffp.rs` (`armcondskip_off_files_every_skip` and the default
    tests), over the `xreffp_arm_le32` fixture this case also loads.

    The XML wrapper only supplies the harness architecture; the pass clears it
    and loads the real linked ARM fixture (built from
    decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/xreffp_arm_le32.c).
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/xreffp_arm_le32</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>load function clamp</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option armcondskip off</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option armcondskip on</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>phase catalog armcondskip</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="KUNA-ARMCONDSKIP #1: the option parses and round-trips in both directions, and is inert on the console path -- clamp's first predicated pair renders identically in all three passes" min="3" max="3">^  if \(a0 &lt; a1\)$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="KUNA-ARMCONDSKIP #2: clamp's second predicated pair renders identically in all three passes" min="3" max="3">^    a0 = a2;$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="KUNA-ARMCONDSKIP #3: the catalog documents it as a default-on option" min="1" max="1">"option": "armcondskip", "values": \["on", "off"\], "default": "on"</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="KUNA-ARMCONDSKIP #4: the catalog row places it in P1 code/data partition" min="1" max="1">"phase": "P1", "subphase": "code-data-partition", "strength": "HARD", "rewind": "P1", "issue": "kuna-analysis-armcondskip"</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
